.\" Hand-written. design/tpm-unlock.md ("Provisioning", "Supported releases", "--server") is the full account.
.TH iron-vault-provision-host-unlock 8 "" "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-provision\-host\-unlock \- seal a host unlock identity to this machine's TPM
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault\-provision\-host\-unlock\fR \fB\-\-server\fR [\fB\-\-accept\-physical\-access\fR]
.br
\fBiron\-vault\-provision\-host\-unlock\fR \fB\-\-portable\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates a host unlock identity with \fBage\-keygen\fR(1) and seals it to the TPM with \fBsystemd\-creds\fR(1),
bound to PCR 7, as \fI/etc/iron\-vault\-host/host\-unlock.cred\fR.
At each boot \fIiron\-vault\-host\-unlock.service\fR unseals it as root and hands it to \fIiron\-vault.service\fR,
which then unlocks the vault with no one present.
The service itself never opens the TPM.
.PP
The secret text exists only in pipes.
Of the identity, only its recipient key is printed, \fBage1\fR..., to enrol with \fBiron\-vault init \-\-host\-unlock\fR or
\fBiron\-vault recipient add \-\-host\-unlock\fR.
The vault passphrase and the offline recovery key keep working: if the unseal ever fails, the service starts Locked
and waits for \fBiron\-vault unlock\fR.
.PP
Run it once, as root.
It refuses to run when the blob already exists; move the old one aside first.
It never clears the TPM, takes ownership, sets hierarchy authorization or changes dictionary\-attack parameters.
.PP
TPM unlock is supported on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS only, and the helper stops on any other release.
.SH OPTIONS
One of \fB\-\-server\fR and \fB\-\-portable\fR is required; there is no default.
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR
For a server or appliance.
Anyone with physical access to the machine and a trusted boot image can start the vault.
The helper says so and seals nothing until you type \fByes\fR at a terminal.
It never reads the answer from a pipe.
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-physical\-access\fR
With \fB\-\-server\fR, accepts that condition without a prompt, for a run with no terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-portable\fR
For a laptop or other portable machine, which needs a full\-disk\-encryption pre\-boot secret as well.
Its check is not built yet, so the helper stops and seals nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the identity is sealed, 1 when the helper stopped, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/iron\-vault\-host/host\-unlock.cred\fR
The host unlock blob: root, mode 0600, in a root 0700 directory.
.TP
\fI/run/iron\-vault\-unlock/host\-unlock\fR
The unlock handoff, on a ramfs, present only while the handoff unit is active.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBiron\-vault\fR(1), \fBiron\-vault\-init\fR(1), \fBiron\-vault\-recipient\-add\fR(1), \fBsystemd\-creds\fR(1)
